# Web Lesson LA12 -- bounded elimination exposes pivots and rank.
# visual: svg
# loops: 0
# **************************************************************************
# * PREREQUISITES -- LA11 system classifications.
# * SHAPES -- A:[equation=2,unknown=2], b:[equation=2], augmented:[row=2,column=3].
# * EXECUTABLE CLAIM -- swap [[0,2|4],[1,1|3]] to safe pivots and reach RREF [[1,0|1],[0,1|2]].
# * NUMERICAL CONTRACT -- exact fixture; CLI requires |pivot|>1e-9 before division.
# * BOUNDARY -- exactly 2x2 with one RHS; this is not stable general Gaussian elimination.
# * WHAT THIS SHOWS -- row swaps avoid zero division, elimination creates pivots, and rank pairs classify solution count.
# **************************************************************************
;
initial = [[0, 2, 4], [1, 1, 3]]  # [A|b] has a zero first pivot
pivoted = [[1, 1, 3], [0, 2, 4]]  # R1 <-> R2
echelon = pivoted  # lower-left entry is already zero
rref = [[1, 0, 1], [0, 1, 2]]  # normalize and eliminate above second pivot
candidate = [1, 2]  # read augmented column
residual = matmul([[0, 2], [1, 1]], candidate) - [4, 3]  # independent [0,0]
rank_unique = [2, 2]  # rank A, rank [A|b]
rank_inconsistent = [1, 2]  # no solution
rank_under = [1, 1]  # infinitely many solutions
disp([initial, pivoted, rref])  # visible row-operation states
equal(residual, [0, 0]) * equal(rank_unique, [2, 2]) * equal(rank_inconsistent, [1, 2]) * equal(rank_under, [1, 1])  # exact claims
# THE VISUAL -- top panels trace swap to RREF; bottom panels map rank pairs to solution counts.
def u:elimination_visual() { "Render the LA12 pivot and rank trace."; "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 980 470\" role=\"img\"><title>Bounded Gaussian elimination exposes pivots and rank</title><desc>A two-by-three augmented matrix swaps rows for a safe pivot and reaches RREF. Rank pairs distinguish unique, inconsistent, and underdetermined systems.</desc><style>text{font-family:monospace;fill:#c0caf5}.p{fill:#24283b;stroke:#414868}.pivot{fill:#e0af68}.ok{fill:#9ece6a}.bad{fill:#f7768e}.arrow{fill:#7aa2f7;font-size:24px}</style><rect width=\"980\" height=\"470\" fill=\"#1a1b26\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"32\">2x2 teaching limit: swap, eliminate, classify rank(A) vs rank([A|b])</text><rect class=\"p\" x=\"20\" y=\"60\" width=\"285\" height=\"220\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"92\">INITIAL [A|b]</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"145\">[ 0  2 | 4 ]</text><text x=\"65\" y=\"190\">[ 1  1 | 3 ]</text><text class=\"pivot\" x=\"50\" y=\"245\">zero pivot: swap rows</text><text class=\"arrow\" x=\"315\" y=\"175\">→</text><rect class=\"p\" x=\"355\" y=\"60\" width=\"285\" height=\"220\"/><text x=\"375\" y=\"92\">ECHELON</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"145\">[ 1  1 | 3 ]</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"190\">[ 0  2 | 4 ]</text><text class=\"ok\" x=\"385\" y=\"245\">safe pivots 1 and 2</text><text class=\"arrow\" x=\"650\" y=\"175\">→</text><rect class=\"p\" x=\"690\" y=\"60\" width=\"270\" height=\"220\"/><text x=\"710\" y=\"92\">RREF</text><text x=\"735\" y=\"145\">[ 1  0 | 1 ]</text><text x=\"735\" y=\"190\">[ 0  1 | 2 ]</text><text class=\"ok\" x=\"725\" y=\"245\">x=[1,2], residual=0</text><rect class=\"p\" x=\"20\" y=\"315\" width=\"940\" height=\"110\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"365\">UNIQUE ranks 2=2</text><text class=\"bad\" x=\"350\" y=\"365\">INCONSISTENT ranks 1&lt;2</text><text class=\"pivot\" x=\"700\" y=\"365\">UNDERDETERMINED ranks 1=1&lt;2</text><text x=\"490\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Every division follows an explicit pivot guard</text></svg>" }  # fixed checked fixture
visual = u:elimination_visual()  # bind once
visual  # display once
# **************************************************************************
# * HOW TO READ THE RESULT -- follow augmented rows left to right; then compare coefficient and augmented ranks below.
# * THE POINT -- pivots encode independent constraints, while guarded row operations preserve solutions.
# **************************************************************************
